# RULE-CONFIRM-KEYS: Escape at a `/permissions` rule confirmation asked
# while a command runs (interrupt-cmd's turns and modes: each product's own
# shell tool under `yolo`, so the command really starts; it sleeps six
# seconds). fx v0.0.16's Escape there is `cancelApprovalOperation`
# (app_input_runtime.zig:2689, :2712-2716@481104fd): the turn is stopped
# and the confirmation goes (input_approval_runtime.zig:401-436). What the
# running command's row says then, and after the six seconds.
fx: gateway interrupt-cmd-fx.json
xfx: gateway interrupt-cmd-xfx.json
fx: env FX_PERMISSION_MODE=yolo
xfx: env XFX_PERMISSION_MODE=yolo
work permissions-early-ws
until shown Full access
wait 2
until gone Full access
type run cmd
key Enter
wait 2
type /permissions remember deny read_file {"path":"a.txt"}
key Enter
until shown 1. Confirm
snap prompt
key Escape
wait 0.6
snap esc
wait 1.5
snap esc-2
wait 4
snap done
